  "id": "memory-storage",
  "term": "memory storage",
  "definition": "Memory storage is the part of working memory that keeps recent information active so it can be used during a task. When this storage demand is reduced, people can maintain better performance for longer on tasks that depend on keeping past choices in mind.",
